# TripodCert — the emitted certificate data (generated by `gen/emit.py`)

Area `Submission/Work/TripodCert/`.  All numbers are mantissas at scale `2^40` (as in the
sibling area `SeedCertRay`), the parameter box is `Work.SeedCertRay.Xb`:

* `dirBaseT` — the six base directions `e^{2πi θ_j}`, `θ_j = T^j(22/63)`;
* `dskT k` — the descent boxes of level `k` (angle-major, `6 × NC` sub-disks);
* `perT` — the *periodic family*: the boxes of all levels `k ≥ KT` (one family, one half-plane
  per angle class) — the fixed point of the cyclic pull-back constraints;
* `crtT k`, `crtPer`, `ifaceCrt` — the (D1) step certificates `(s, ρ, M)`;
* `dirT k`, `dirPer`, `ifaceDir` — the (D2) half-plane directions;
* `Uzx/Uzy/URm` — the rational disc used by the uniqueness certificate.
-/
import Mathlib
import Submission.Work.TripodCert.Num

-- Lean v4.35.0-rc3 / Mathlib 5e0c4e5 made `isDefEq` respect transparency when unifying instances; with it,
-- `ZMod.instField` and `ZMod.commRing` (and `Neg (ZMod p)` via `SubtractionMonoid`) no longer unify, which
-- breaks `ring`/`rw`/module-instance search on `ZMod p`. Restore the v4.34 behaviour for this file.
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.instanceSearchTypes false
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false


namespace Work.TripodCert

open Work.SeedCertRay

